      "math_academy_id": "q-265764",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Compute the gradient of the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]x\n$$\n\n with respect to $x$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Writing $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}Ax.\n$$\n\nFor a symmetric matrix $A$, the gradient of the function $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax$ with respect to $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=2Ax.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $A$ is symmetric, we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=2[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
